KG42.register("clusters-9d7da6e7e25fef86a9f6c78a",{"id":"40-fair_dso_flexibility::v142-d-CL002","paper":"40-fair_dso_flexibility","label":"pay-as-bid simulation benchmark compensation","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-CL002","label":"pay-as-bid simulation benchmark compensation","market_meaning":"In the M02 simulation benchmark, the DSO calculates payments based on the flexibility costs declared by aggregators and measured actions. This chain has an independent compensation meaning, but the time aggregation, units and experimental tolerance interpretation of the payment still need clarification.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M02"],"market_types":["DEM"],"process_stages":["settlement"],"scope_disposition":"compatible","scope_explanation":"The sole bound chain is limited to the pay-as-bid benchmark scenario of M02, and there is no cross-mechanism merging within the cluster. The original payment expression and experimental scope are retained; no definitions are completed by borrowing M01's cost function, ECPM penalties or incentive properties.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"Declared costs, measured actions, DSO payment activities and compensation results constitute an independent benchmark payment rule. Sharing generic nodes or symbols with M01 is insufficient to establish the same payment rule or cross-mechanism quantity identity, so it is retained separately.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R004","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"The single chain already provides the inputs, executing entity and payment expression of benchmark compensation; its unclosed aspects are explicitly recorded as gaps."}],"connections":[],"object_mappings":[],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G001","category":"unverified_source","description":"E26 and E27 remain unverified, and the existing C2 revision request also requires checking the payment expression, symbol domain, units and benchmark scope. Admission of this round's experiment cannot replace source audit or scientific confirmation.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-X001","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-X002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E26","v141-b-g02-E27"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the original payment formula and experimental context, and conduct manual scientific review of this chain and the single-chain cluster."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G002","category":"math_incomplete","description":"The payment p_i has no time-period index, whereas both inputs carry t; the source does not clarify whether this is a single-period payment or a full-horizon payment, nor does it explain the input units, normalization or time aggregation. The existing chain is not yet sufficient to provide a complete settlement basis.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-X001","v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-X002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E26","v141-b-g02-E27"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Upstream should verify the payment time range, symbol units and aggregation conventions; retain the current formula, and do not automatically import definitions from M01 or fabricate a summation."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-CL002-G003","category":"scope_conflict","description":"The 0.05% tolerance wording in E27 is inconsistent with the simultaneously listed δ_K values of 0.95, 1 and 1.05. This ambiguity affects the interpretation of the deviation range in the benchmark experiment, and no new tolerance or performance obligation may be added on its basis.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R004"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-X002","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-E27"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Verify the source-text correspondence among the tolerance wording, percentage and deviation factor, and clarify the experimental scope; D does not choose one numerical interpretation."}]},"rule_refs":["40-fair_dso_flexibility::v141-c-R004"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-2520bc1d04369b56","COMP-f1a6e363e99ce7b8"]});
